-- title:
--   Tame j-finite places of X(Γ₁(M)∩Γ₀(p)) unramified over X₀(Mp)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $K_1$ and $K_2$ be intermediate fields of $L \subseteq L((q))$, where $K_1$ is the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise images under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by all quotients $p_f/p_g$ of integral $q$-expansions of two modular forms of one and the same weight for $\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p)$ (with $p_g \ne 0$), and $K_2$ is the corresponding field built from $\Gamma_0(Mp)$; assume $K_2 \le K_1$. Let $J \in K_1$ be the element whose underlying Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of $q^{-1}$ times the integral power series $j$-numerator, i.e. of the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant. Let $x$ be a place of $K_1$ over $L$ — a proper valuation subring of $K_1$ containing $L$ and a principal ideal ring — with associated order function $\operatorname{ord}_x$, and assume $0 \le \operatorname{ord}_x J$; assume further that $\operatorname{ord}_x J > 0$ forces $p \not\equiv 1 \pmod 3$ together with the implication that $p = 3$ only if some prime $\ell \mid M$ has $\ell \not\equiv 1 \pmod 3$, and that $\operatorname{ord}_x (J - 1728) > 0$ forces $p \not\equiv 1 \pmod 4$ together with the implication that $p = 2$ only if some prime $\ell \mid M$ has $\ell \not\equiv 1 \pmod 4$. Then the ramification index of $x$ along the inclusion $K_2 \hookrightarrow K_1$, namely the least $n > 0$ of the form $\operatorname{ord}_x f$ for some nonzero $f \in K_2$, equals $1$.
--
--   This is the horizontal unramifiedness statement for the covering $X(\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p)) \to X_0(Mp)$ of modular curves, expressed through their function fields realised as $q$-expansion fields inside $L((q))$: away from the cusps (places where $j$ has nonnegative order) and under congruence conditions at $p$ ruling out elliptic points of $\Gamma_0(Mp)$ of order $3$ and $2$, the covering is unramified. It feeds [`ModularCurve.exists_ord_eq_one_of_place_x1x0FunctionFieldC_gamma0_of_ord_nonneg_of_tame`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_ord_eq_one_of_place_x1x0FunctionFieldC_gamma0_of_ord_nonneg_of_tame), which produces a uniformiser coming from the lower field, in the analysis of the modular tower used for level structures at $p$.
